/* book exam traps: Module uses the pitch circle: m = d/z. Using the tip (addendum) diameter or the base diameter gives a wrong module. | Contact ratio is the path of contact over the base pitch πm cos φ, or the arc of contact over p = πm; a path over p is wrong. | The law of gearing is about the common normal at the contact point, not the common tangent. Examiners test this wording. | Diametral pitch is in inch units: P = z/d with d in inches, and m = 25.4/P. Mixing mm with P gives nonsense. | Undercutting is not a cure; it is the damage interference causes when a pinion has too few teeth. The cures are more teeth, a profile shift or a stub tooth. */
