/* book exam traps: The beam strength σb b m Y is a capacity, not the applied load. Compare it with fs times the effective load. | Putting d1 in mm into v = πd1n/60: v comes out 1000 times too large. | Mixing the two Lewis forms: Y (about 0.3) goes with σb b m Y; y = Y/π (about 0.1) goes with σb b πm y. | Using Cv and Buckingham's Fd together: Cv is for the first sizing only; then Feff = Cs Ft + Fd. | Checking only bending. In many designs wear governs, as in the second example; the cure is surface hardness, not a larger module. */
